  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>At 42 Nouveau Port in Cavalaire-sur-Mer, Le Bateau Ivre is a brasserie set in the middle of the harbour, with a 180° terrace facing the boats. Golfe de Saint-Tropez Tourisme presents it as a bar-brasserie with a musical atmosphere and themed evenings, serving breakfasts, ice creams, crêpes, waffles and cocktails. The menu mixes seafood (whole sea bass, smoked salmon, prawns, baby squid with parsley) and Italian and Mediterranean specialities (gnocchi, penne, risotto).</p>

      <h2>Dog policy</h2>
      <p>The Cavalaire tourist office, in its listing relayed by Provence-Alpes-Côte d'Azur Tourisme and Golfe de Saint-Tropez Tourisme, says "animals accepted". No more precise rule (terrace only, size, surcharge) is published. The terrace facing the harbour is the simplest choice with a dog. As the venue offers music and themed evenings, a noise-sensitive dog will probably be more comfortable at breakfast or lunchtime.</p>

      <h2>Practical information</h2>
      <p>The tourist office listing (updated 11 May 2026) announces opening all year, every day; the establishment's website gives hours of 8am to 10:30pm. The phone number on the Golfe de Saint-Tropez listing is 07 63 85 98 70. On the legal side, the company Le Bateau Ivre has been registered at this address since July 2024, for a bar, brasserie, restaurant and takeaway activity.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: in summer, choose a table in the shade and bring water for your dog if you stop by in the middle of the day.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Cavalaire harbour and its promenade are great for a walk before or after the meal.</p>
